from pydantic.dataclasses import dataclass


StrictConfig = ConfigDict(str_strip_whitespace=True, validate_assignment=True)


@dataclass(config=StrictConfig)", "explanation": "Pydantic V2 replaces class-based `config` with a `ConfigDict` (migration.md#changes-to-config: config is set via a dict-style config, the v1 `Config` class pattern is deprecated). The class-based StrictConfig is replaced by a ConfigDict passed to @dataclass. Also, `anystr_strip_whitespace` was renamed to `str_strip_whitespace` per the documented rename list, so the stripping behavior is preserved. `validate_assignment` is unchanged. `ConfigDict` is imported for use."}], "notes": "Fixed the class-based config deprecation in app/geo.py with a single edit: StrictConfig is now a ConfigDict using the renamed key str_strip_whitespace (was anystr_strip_whitespace) and validate_assignment, passed to @dataclass(config=...). Behavior risk NOT addressed by this edit (outside the listed finding): `__post_init_post_parse__` is a Pydantic V1 dataclass hook. Pydantic V2 does not call it; it uses `__post_init__` instead. Because it is not a finding, I left it unchanged. Renaming it would change when the normalization runs, so it should be verified by the tests, not guessed at. Tests may fail on the coordinate range check and title-casing if this hook is no longer called."}
